%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
Testing grounds to see if 3.6m cube can run with concrete and get visible Ascan results. 
Currently, it takes ~30 minutes to run one of these Ascans with 1cm dx, though it might need to be finer.
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

%%%% Testing if can see results with 65ns instead of 30! Try with and without sphere! %%%%
#title: A-scan of 3.6m cube with sphere in air


@@ General Setup @@
#domain: 3.6 3.6 3.6
This^ is the bounds of the sim in meters.

%% #dx_dy_dz: 0.02 0.02 0.02
#dx_dy_dz: 0.01 0.01 0.01
%% #dx_dy_dz: 0.01 0.01 0.01 << this size discretization takes 10 min to run the simulation, which is just half the og size. 
^Discrete chunks of the sim, also in meters

%% #time_window: 30e-9
#time_window: 65e-9
^half space with permittivity of 6 needs 60ns!!!
/#time_window: 20e-9
In seconds of the sim^


@@ Materials @@
#material: 5 5 1 3 concrete
%% #material: 3 0.01 1 0 my_sand
/#material: 1 0 1 0 air 
/#material: 6 .10 1 0 wet_asphalt
/#material: 6 0 1 0 half_space
^epsilon, conductivity, mu, magnetic loss, name

@Makeup of Box@
%% #box: 0 0 0 3.6 3.2 3.6 free_space
#box: 0 0 0 3.6 3.2 3.6 concrete
%% #box: 0 0 0 3.6 3.2 3.6 my_sand
^Current problem: free space sees 5% error, but sand sees -20% error. What's going on here?
Makes a box of a specified material^

@Sphere calibration tests (for centered, leave x and z coords)@
%% 50cm sphere %%
%% #sphere: 1.700 1.600 1.700 0.500 pec n
^50cm radius sphere 1m away
%% #sphere: 1.700 0.600 1.700 0.500 pec n
^50cm radius sphere 2m away
%%#sphere: 1.700 0.001 1.700 0.500 pec n
^50cm radius sphere 3m away (yes, this radius size won't work)

%% 20cm sphere %%
%% #sphere: 1.800 1.300 1.800 0.200 pec n
^20cm radius sphere 1m away
%% #sphere: 1.800 1.300 1.800 0.200 pec n
^20cm radius sphere 2m away
%% #sphere: 1.800 0.300 1.800 0.200 pec n
^20cm radius sphere 3m away (yes, this radius size won't work)

%% 10cm sphere %%
%% #sphere: 1.800 2.300 1.800 0.100 pec n
^20cm radius sphere 1m away
%% #sphere: 1.800 1.300 1.800 0.100 pec n
^20cm radius sphere 2m away
#sphere: 1.800 0.300 1.800 0.100 pec n
^20cm radius sphere 3m away (yes, this radius size won't work)  <<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< currently running the 10cm radius sphere 3m away from the rx/tx

@Cylinder/pipe tests@
/#cylinder: 1.000 1.000 0.2 1.000 1.000 0.7 0.50 pec n
^this was totally 2m away, NOT 1m, which is why our reflection came in at 15 ns not 10 like it should at 1m!!!!
/#cylinder: 1.800 1.000 0.200 1.800 1.000 0.700 0.500 pec n
^Cylinder centered with top and bottom coords and .5m radius, perfect electric conductor with
 no dielectric smoothing (not far enough out to need it or with resistive enough material to pass through)
/#cylinder: 2.250 1.000 0.200 2.250 1.000 0.700 0.050 pec n
^clean spacing for 1/10 size at 5cm not 50
/#cylinder: 1.250 1.000 0.200 1.250 1.000 0.700 0.050 pec n
^clean spacing but back a meter for smaller domain!
/#cylinder: 1.125 2.325 0.1 1.125 2.375 0.8 0.50 wet_asphalt n
Makes a sphere at ^ with radius of .25m of 
a Perfect Electric Conductor and no dielectric smoothing
^REMEMBER any time you change radius, reposition so still 1m away or chosen distance


@@ EM Wave stuff @@
#waveform: ricker 1 1e9 my_pulse


%% #hertzian_dipole: z 1.500 3.100 1.700 my_pulse     
^40cm apart rx and tx
#hertzian_dipole: z 1.650 3.400 1.700 my_pulse     
^30cm apart rx and tx
^ These make the pulse source and place it in the sim.



%% #rx: 1.900 3.100 1.700 
^40cm apart rx and tx
#rx: 1.950 3.400 1.700 
^30cm apart rx and tx

/#rx: 3.375 1.075 0.75 Ex Ey Ez (only gives these parts, but still need to use --outputs Ez -fft for the graph and FFT)
^ Location of the receiver


@@ PML @@
#pml_cells: 5
^^^ so far, I can't see much difference between 5 cells and 10, so unless necessary, leave at 5 to allow for more working room


@@ Viewing the model @@
/#geometry_view: 0 0 0 4 2 1 0.02 0.02 0.02 cyl_3m_cube n
#geometry_view: 0 0 0 3.6 3.6 3.6 0.02 0.02 0.02 large_3point6m_cube n
^adjusted for new 1m smaller domain in x direc
^position, discretization, filename, and normal not fine so smaller filesize
